      "id": "claim_6655acec504a402a912c90ad3776e2fa",
      "statement": "The client side of the chat code stream is ChatOtClient, a two-buffer OT client holding at most one in-flight submitCodeChange plus one composed pending buffer of newer local edits, both transformed against incoming remote rows; submissions land at round-trip granularity, retry the same (clientId, seq) with an identical payload on transport failure (the server dedupe digest requires it), and base content is only ever fetched from getCodeAtCommit or the displayed head tree.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-frontend/src/otClient.ts#L113-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e61b64a31536f4488ab20f84c747a9cab16b4aaf6987b92172417512f9b3ea0a:"
